# Cursor AI Rules for OptiAI Project

## Project Overview
OptiAI is an AI-powered desktop system optimizer built with React (frontend), Python FastAPI (backend), and Tauri (desktop wrapper).

## Architecture Principles
- Follow single responsibility principle - each file/class should do one thing
- Keep files under 500 lines, split immediately if approaching 400 lines
- Use object-oriented design with dedicated classes for each functionality
- Favor composition over inheritance
- Build for reuse, not just to "make it work"

## Code Organization
- UI logic -> ViewModel/Manager
- Business logic -> Manager/Service
- Navigation/state flow -> Coordinator
- Never mix views and business logic directly
- Use descriptive, intention-revealing names
- Avoid vague names like "data", "info", "helper"

## Technology Stack
- Frontend: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion
- Backend: Python FastAPI
- Desktop: Tauri (Rust)
- Database: JSON files + secure vault storage
- AI: Ollama/local LLM integration

## Security & Policy
- All actions must be validated through policy.yaml
- Never bypass PolicyManager validation
- No shell commands in action execution (Python stdlib only)
- Protected paths are immutable
- All LLM outputs must pass policy validation

## Development Guidelines
- Use TypeScript for new components (Processes.tsx, Startup.tsx pattern)
- Prefer pure HTML/JS/CSS for UI features without external libraries
- API communication via fetch to http://127.0.0.1:5174
- Follow existing patterns in components/ directory
- Maintain comprehensive undo functionality for all actions

## Testing & Quality
- Write tests for all new functionality
- Use pytest for Python backend tests
- Maintain test coverage above 80%
- Run integration tests before deployment
- Validate all schemas against JSON schemas in schemas/ directory

## Performance
- Optimize for desktop performance
- Use lazy loading for large components
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Monitor memory usage in long-running operations
- Cache API responses appropriately

## File Structure
- src/components/ - React components
- src/pages/ - Page components (TypeScript preferred)
- src/hooks/ - Custom React hooks
- src/utils/ - Utility functions
- src/context/ - React context providers
- backend/ - Python FastAPI backend
- src-tauri/ - Tauri desktop wrapper
- scripts/ - Build and utility scripts

## API Endpoints
- POST /api/scan - Start filesystem scan
- GET /api/scan/{scan_id}/status - Check scan progress
- POST /api/optimize - Generate AI suggestions
- POST /api/action - Execute actions with validation
- POST /api/undo - Undo actions
- GET /api/actions/history - Action audit log

## Ports & Configuration
- Backend API: 5174
- Frontend Vite dev: 3001
- Ollama LLM: 11434
- Tauri dev: Dynamic assignment

## Error Handling
- Use proper error boundaries in React
- Implement graceful fallbacks for external tools
- Log all errors with context
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Maintain action history for debugging

## Documentation
- Comment complex algorithms
- Document API endpoints
- Maintain README files
- Update CHANGELOG for releases
- Document security policies

## Git Workflow
- Use conventional commits
- Create feature branches
- Run tests before merging
- Update documentation with changes
- Tag releases appropriately
